warning[pointer_lifetime]: `p` points into `xs`, which may be resized: f(*xs); possible targets of `f`: grow, other_grow; the labelled chain identifies an invalidating target; shortest bad path shown (0 other bad paths)
  --> tests/lint/pointer_lifetime/strict/calls.jai:25:10
   |
 3 | grow :: (xs: *[..] int) {} @GrowsArray
   |         ------------------ possible procedure target
 4 | other_grow :: (xs: *[..] int) {} @GrowsArray
   |               ------------------ possible procedure target
   ...
22 |     p := *xs[0];
   |          ------ pointer derived here
   ...
24 |     f(*xs);
   |     ------ `xs` storage invalidated here
25 |     sink(p);
   |          ^ pointer used here after its storage was invalidated
   |
   = help: take the pointer again after growth, or store an index instead
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/pointer_lifetime

